CLASS BaseComponent
    DESCRIPTION: Base class for all component models sent to servers
    NAMESPACE: NewgroundsIO
    EXTENDS: BaseObject
    
    PURPOSE: Components are the building blocks of API calls. Every action you send to
    the server (unlock a medal, post a score, check session, etc.) is done via a component.
    This base class provides common functionality for all component types.
    
    KEY CONCEPT: Components are OUTGOING - sent FROM the app TO the server.
    (Results are the INCOMING response FROM server TO app)
    
    WHY SEPARATE CLASS: Components have special requirements that regular models don't:
    - Some must be encrypted before transmission
    - Some require a session id; some additionally require a validated login
    - Some open browser windows (redirects)
    - Some need special validation (can't execute without a valid session)
    
    COMPONENT HIERARCHY:
    - BaseComponent is the foundation
    - All specific components (Medal.unlock, ScoreBoard.postScore, etc.) extend BaseComponent
    - Each component defines its own properties and requirements
    
    ====================
    PUBLIC PROPERTIES (beyond BaseObject)
    ====================
    
    isSecure: boolean = false
        PURPOSE: Whether this component must be encrypted before sending
        WHY: Sensitive operations like unlocking medals or posting scores are encrypted
        to prevent hackers from cheating
        ENCRYPTION PROCESS: When true, the component is encrypted using the app's
        encryption key before being sent to the server
        WHEN TRUE: Medal.unlock, ScoreBoard.postScore, ScoreBoard operations
        WHEN FALSE: Read-only operations like Medal.getList, ScoreBoard.getBoards
    
    requiresSession: boolean = false
        PURPOSE: Whether a session ID must be present in the request envelope
        WHY: The gateway rejects these with 102 when no session id is sent
        SCHEMA: model.require_session
        VALIDATION: If requiresSession=true and there is no session ID,
        getPreflightError() refuses the component before it is sent.
        NOTE: this flag means LITERALLY "a session id must be sent", and nothing
        more. Whether anyone is signed in is requiresLogin's question.

    requiresLogin: boolean = false
        PURPOSE: Whether a VALIDATED LOGIN is required, not merely a session id
        WHY: A guest session has a real id belonging to nobody. It satisfies
        require_session, and the gateway still refuses these with 110.
        SCHEMA: model.require_login
        EXAMPLES:
            - requiresLogin=true: Medal.unlock, ScoreBoard.postScore, CloudSave.*
            - requiresLogin=false: App.checkSession - its whole job is to find
              out whether anyone has signed in yet, so requiring a login would
              make signing in impossible
        VALIDATION: If requiresLogin=true and the session carries no user,
        getPreflightError() refuses the component with LOGIN_REQUIRED (110).
        NOT A PARAMETER: this does not mean "pass a user object". The flag is
        named require_login rather than require_user for exactly that reason -
        the latter read like an argument the caller had to supply.
        ABSENT MEANS FALSE. Schemas published before this flag existed do not
        carry it, so a component is only gated once the gateway says so.
        NEVER DERIVE THIS FROM require_session. See getPreflightError() below.
    
    redirect: boolean = false
        PURPOSE: Whether this component opens a browser window
        WHY: Loader components may send the player to a URL
        rather than exchanging JSON
        REDIRECT PROCESS: When true, instead of making AJAX request with JSON,
        the browser is redirected to the gateway with component data in URL
        EXAMPLES:
            - Loader.openOfficialUrl opens a browser destination
            - Once complete, window closes and session is updated
        WHEN TRUE: Loader.* components
        NAMING: this property is `redirect`, NOT `isRedirect`. It is read by name
        from outside the model - the request pipeline branches on
        `componentModel.redirect` - so the name is part of the contract
        NOTE: For Loader components this same property is also a real server
        parameter. Keep it in propertyNames for those components so `redirect:false`
        reaches the gateway when requesting URL data instead of a browser redirect.

    browserTarget: string | null = null
        PURPOSE: The window/frame to open redirect in (if redirect=true)
        WHY: Specifies where the browser window/tab should open
        VALUES:
            - "_blank": Open in new window/tab
            - "_self": Replace current window
            - "_parent": Open in parent frame
            - "_top": Open at top level
        DEFAULT: null
        WHY NULL: the component does not choose its own target. The NGIO wrapper
        methods supply one at call time (they pass "_blank"), so a default here
        would silently override the caller's choice

    ====================
    CONSTRUCTOR
    ====================
    
    CONSTRUCTOR()
        
        PURPOSE: Initialize the component with default property values
        
        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: Call parent constructor
            CALL super()
            
            COMMENT: Set component-specific defaults
            SET this.isSecure TO false
            SET this.requiresSession TO false
            SET this.requiresLogin TO false
            SET this.redirect TO false
            SET this.browserTarget TO null
    END CONSTRUCTOR
    
    ====================
    OVERRIDDEN METHODS
    ====================
    
    FUNCTION getPreflightError(): NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Error | null

        PURPOSE: Enhanced validation that includes the session requirement
        WHY: Core calls this BEFORE SENDING, so a component that cannot possibly
        succeed is refused without spending a network round trip.

        Return the code the GATEWAY would have returned for the same condition -
        MISSING_PARAMETER (102) for no session id, LOGIN_REQUIRED (110) for a
        session with no validated login - so callers cannot tell a local refusal
        from a server one except by how fast it arrives. See the contract note in
        Core.pseudo.

        ====================================================================
        TWO FLAGS, AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME QUESTION
        ====================================================================

        require_session -> requiresSession
            A SESSION ID MUST BE SENT. Literally that, and nothing more.
            Refused with MISSING_PARAMETER (102).

        require_login   -> requiresLogin
            A VALIDATED LOGIN IS REQUIRED. A guest session - a real id belonging
            to nobody - satisfies require_session and fails this.
            Refused with LOGIN_REQUIRED (110).

        WHY THERE ARE TWO, and the history is worth keeping because the
        single-flag version looked perfectly reasonable:

        The gateway has always checked these two things separately and
        correctly. THE SCHEMA was what conflated them. A single require_session
        flag was used where require_login is used now, so one flag carried both
        meanings and nothing downstream could tell them apart.

        A library reading that flag as "needs a logged-in user" was matching
        what it then meant - but App.checkSession was marked with it despite
        needing no login at all, so enforcing it before sending WOULD HAVE MADE
        SIGN-IN IMPOSSIBLE: the call whose job is to discover whether anyone has
        signed in would be refused for the absence of exactly that.

        The lesson for your port is not "the old libraries were careless". It is
        that A FLAG WITH TWO MEANINGS CANNOT BE ENFORCED, and that the bug stayed
        invisible for as long as nothing acted on it. Enforcement is what made
        the ambiguity a real problem, and therefore what got it fixed.

        ABSENT MEANS FALSE: a schema without require_login gates nothing, and the
        server keeps making that call. NEVER re-derive requiresLogin from
        requiresSession.

        RETURNS: An Error describing the first problem found, or null

        EXPLANATION:
            This method enhances BaseObject.getPreflightError() with extra checks:
            1. First runs the parent validation (check required properties)
            2. Then checks component-specific requirements (session validation)

        BEHAVIOR:
            COMMENT: ==================== RUN PARENT VALIDATION ====================
            COMMENT: Check all the basic required properties first
            CREATE parentError AS CALL super.getPreflightError()
            IF parentError is not null THEN
                COMMENT: Parent validation failed - this component is incomplete
                RETURN parentError
            END IF

            COMMENT: ==================== CHECK SESSION REQUIREMENT ====================
            IF this.requiresSession is true THEN
                COMMENT: This component needs a session id in the envelope.
                COMMENT: Everything below means there is no id to send, so the
                COMMENT: gateway would answer 102 - and that answer needs no
                COMMENT: request to obtain.

                COMMENT: First check if core is available
                IF this.core is null THEN
                    COMMENT: No core reference - can't check session
                    RETURN sessionError(Errors.MISSING_PARAMETER, "has no Core to read a session from")
                END IF

                COMMENT: Check if appState is available
                IF this.core.appState is null THEN
                    COMMENT: No app state - can't check session
                    RETURN sessionError(Errors.MISSING_PARAMETER, "has no app state to read a session from")
                END IF

                COMMENT: Get the current session from app state
                CREATE session AS this.core.appState.session

                COMMENT: Validate the session exists
                IF session is null THEN
                    COMMENT: No session at all - can't execute
                    RETURN sessionError(Errors.MISSING_PARAMETER, "requires a session, and there is none")
                END IF

                COMMENT: Validate that session has an ID.
                COMMENT:
                COMMENT: A session id with no user attached is a GUEST session,
                COMMENT: which satisfies require_session. Whether it is ENOUGH is
                COMMENT: require_login's question, handled in the next block. Do
                COMMENT: NOT add a session.user check here - collapsing the two
                COMMENT: flags back together is what makes sign-in impossible.
                IF session.id is null OR session.id is empty THEN
                    COMMENT: No session token - can't execute
                    RETURN sessionError(Errors.MISSING_PARAMETER, "requires a session id, and the session has none")
                END IF
            END IF

            COMMENT: ==================== CHECK LOGIN REQUIREMENT ====================
            COMMENT: Deliberately INDEPENDENT of the block above rather than
            COMMENT: nested inside it. A component needing a login needs a session
            COMMENT: id by definition, but reading that dependency out of the
            COMMENT: schema is the gateway's job, not an inference to make here -
            COMMENT: and if a component ever carries require_login without
            COMMENT: require_session, the honest answer is still "not logged in".
            IF this.requiresLogin is true THEN
                IF this.core is null OR this.core.appState is null THEN
                    RETURN sessionError(Errors.LOGIN_REQUIRED, "requires a logged-in user, and there is no app state to read a session from")
                END IF

                CREATE loginSession AS this.core.appState.session

                IF loginSession is null OR loginSession.user is null THEN
                    COMMENT: Either no session at all, or a GUEST session - the id
                    COMMENT: is real and belongs to nobody. The gateway says 110.
                    RETURN sessionError(Errors.LOGIN_REQUIRED, "requires a logged-in user, and this session has none")
                END IF

                IF loginSession.user.id is null OR loginSession.user.id is empty THEN
                    RETURN sessionError(Errors.LOGIN_REQUIRED, "requires a logged-in user, and this session's user has no id")
                END IF
            END IF

            COMMENT: ==================== ALL VALIDATION PASSED ====================
            COMMENT: Component is properly formatted and can be executed
            RETURN null
    END FUNCTION

    FUNCTION sessionError(code: integer, problem: string): NewgroundsIO.models.objects.Error

        PURPOSE: Build a session-requirement error naming this component.

        BEHAVIOR:
            RETURN Errors.getError(code, getFullObjectName() + " " + problem + ".")
    END FUNCTION
    
    ====================
    HOW A COMPONENT IDENTIFIES ITSELF
    ====================

    COMMENT: BaseComponent adds NO identity method of its own. A component identifies
    COMMENT: itself through the same abstract members every model overrides, inherited
    COMMENT: from BaseObject: objectName, objectType, propertyNames, requiredProperties
    COMMENT: and castTypes. Do not invent a component-only accessor for this.
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: For components the two identity members are:
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT:    objectName -> the FULL component path, "Component.method"
    COMMENT:                  e.g. "Medal.unlock", "App.checkSession", "CloudSave.setData"
    COMMENT:    objectType -> "component"
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: The full path is load-bearing, not decorative. Execute.setComponent() copies
    COMMENT: objectName straight into the wire payload as the `component` field:
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT:    SET this.component TO componentModel.objectName
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: The gateway routes on that string. Returning just the method name ("unlock")
    COMMENT: produces a request the server cannot dispatch, and the failure surfaces as a
    COMMENT: server-side error rather than anything the client can point at.

    ====================
    COMPONENT EXECUTION FLOW (FOR DEVELOPERS)
    ====================
    
    COMMENT: Understanding how a component gets executed:
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 1: Create the component
    COMMENT:    var component = new Medal.unlock()
    COMMENT:    component.id = 5
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 2: (Optional) Queue it or execute immediately
    COMMENT:    NGIO.core.queueComponent(component)
    COMMENT:    NGIO.core.executeQueue(onComplete)
    COMMENT:    OR
    COMMENT:    NGIO.core.executeComponent(component, onComplete)
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 3: Core wraps it in an Execute object
    COMMENT:    var execute = new Execute()
    COMMENT:    execute.setComponent(component)
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 4: Core wraps all executes in a Request object
    COMMENT:    var request = new Request()
    COMMENT:    request.setExecute([execute1, execute2])
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 5: Request converts to plain object (triggering encryption if needed)
    COMMENT:    This is where:
    COMMENT:    - isSecure components get encrypted
    COMMENT:    - Properties are validated
    COMMENT:    - The request is prepared for transmission
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 6: Request is converted to JSON and sent via HTTP POST
    COMMENT:    JSON is sent to gateway_v3.php on Newgrounds server
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 7: Server processes the components
    COMMENT:    - Validates that properties are correct
    COMMENT:    - Decrypts any secure components
    COMMENT:    - Executes the component logic (unlock medal, post score, etc.)
    COMMENT:    - Generates a Result object with the outcome
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 8: Server returns JSON response
    COMMENT:    Response contains:
    COMMENT:    - success flag (true/false)
    COMMENT:    - result object (specific to the component type)
    COMMENT:    - error object (if success=false)
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 9: Core parses the response
    COMMENT:    - Response object is created and populated from JSON
    COMMENT:    - AppState is updated with any new data
    COMMENT:    - Result objects are created and populated
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: STEP 10: Callback is invoked with the Response
    COMMENT:    Developer's callback is called with the results
    COMMENT:    Developer can check result.success and react appropriately
    
    ====================
    IMPORTANT DESIGN NOTES
    ====================
    
    COMMENT: Session Validation Timing:
    COMMENT:   The requiresSession check happens in getPreflightError()
    COMMENT:   Core calls it BEFORE sending to the server, so a component with
    COMMENT:   no session id to send is refused locally and no network request
    COMMENT:   is wasted on an impossible operation.
    COMMENT:   A GUEST session (id present, nobody signed in) is refused here too
    COMMENT:   when the component sets requiresLogin, with LOGIN_REQUIRED (110).
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: Encryption:
    COMMENT:   If isSecure=true, the component is encrypted by Core.encryptData()
    COMMENT:   This prevents cheaters from modifying the component in transit
    COMMENT:   Example: Medal unlock rewards must be encrypted or hacker could fake it
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: Redirects:
    COMMENT:   Some components (the Loader family) use redirect=true
    COMMENT:   These don't get responses back to the app
    COMMENT:   Instead, the browser is redirected to complete the action
    COMMENT:   After redirect completes, session is updated server-side
    COMMENT:   App detects the change on next checkSession() call
    COMMENT:
    COMMENT: Server-Side Validation:
    COMMENT:   Just because a component passes getPreflightError() locally doesn't mean
    COMMENT:   the server will accept it. The server does additional validation:
    COMMENT:   - Are values in valid range?
    COMMENT:   - Does the medal/scoreboard exist?
    COMMENT:   - Does the user have permission? (INCLUDING "is this guest session
    COMMENT:     enough?", which the preflight check deliberately does not judge)
    COMMENT:   If server rejects it, the result.error will contain the reason

END CLASS
